    {
      "index": 6,
      "field": {
        "path": "website/content/publications/pbps-centered-macro-defect-gap.json",
        "pointer": "/items/0/statement",
        "value": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including rank zero as an explicit extension of the source Euclidean setting. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, 0<α≤β, and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v. Let η>0 and βη≤1. Set μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=Law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd. Let P be the actual conditional-expectation orthogonal projection onto the second-coordinate sigma algebra in L²(J). There exists one linear isometry U:L²(J)→L²(J) whose AE representative is composition with F(x,y)=(x,2x−y), with U²=I and U self-adjoint. Define A=PUP and B=(I−P)UP. For every f∈ran P with ∫f dJ=0, ‖Af‖≤[(1−αη)/(1+αη)]‖f‖ and [4αη/(1+αη)²]‖f‖²≤‖Bf‖². This includes αη=1, uses the actual, potentially infinite-dimensional L²(J), without imposing finite-dimensionality on L², and is Test-level integration of already produced operators; Γ, its inverse and trajectories are not asserted."
      },
      "whole_value_utf8_bytes": 1013,
      "whole_value_utf8_sha256": "fe3d0629218e20c35114311717ec09fe09be6a27f9b275579a435f3156c66e7e",
      "verdict": "QUALIFIED_POTENTIAL_DIMENSION_CORRECT",
      "semantic_review": "Explicitly allows rank zero and states no finite-dimensionality imposed on L2. Complete reflected-law/contraction statement retains source hypotheses and Test/Gamma boundary."
    },
