    {
      "index": 19,
      "field": {
        "path": "research-wiki/semantic-roundtrip/audits/ASTIS-RT-20261008-L2PullbackRange.json",
        "pointer": "/source/original_text",
        "value": "Attributed ASTIS-authored scoped mathematical restatement/completion.\nLet X,Y be arbitrary measurable spaces, μ,ν arbitrary measures and f:X→Y measure preserving (measurable and f₊μ=ν). Let M_f:L²(ν;ℝ)→L²(μ;ℝ) be canonical isometric pullback. Then its range is exactly the submodule of L²(μ;ℝ) classes having an AE strongly measurable representative for the comap sigma algebra f⁻¹ΣY. There is no probability, finite-measure, standard-Borel or finite-dimensional hypothesis.\nExact source boundary: PBPS2609.06905v1 AppendixB B1-B5 exact macro identification/centering feeding C3-C4 and B15. Public actual canonical pullback range=P range and centered image equality; real new Test transports exact57 scalar contraction to all actual centered macro f and squared defect gap.\nRemaining: PBPS2609.06905v1 AppendixB B1-B5 exact macro identification/centering feeding C3-C4 and B15. Public actual canonical pullback range=P range and centered image equality; real new Test transports exact57 scalar contraction to all actual centered macro f and squared defect gap. Finite real Hilbert/Borel/rank0 explicit extension; trueL2 generally infinite dimensional. Public generic pullback range and actual PBPS range/mean/centered image; realTest-only allmacro contraction/squaredBgap. NoGamma/fullweakH1/B13/B14/dynamics/main/cost/composition/fullpaper/Goal claim."
